{
  "$comment": [
    "Conformance vectors for SPEC §4.2 — the normative derivation of axes.blast_radius.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. blast_radius is the only axis that selects between",
    "require_approval (R2, broad) and deny (R3, systemic), and until this file existed",
    "each adapter derived it its own way: the WordPress reference adapter by substring",
    "matching on the ability name, the Claude Code reference adapter from the shape of",
    "the command's target. SPEC §7 has always said an adapter 'MUST pass the conformance",
    "suite' for the axes; for this axis there was no suite to pass. RFX-131.",
    "",
    "HOW A CASE IS WRITTEN. `given` states the situation ABSTRACTLY — what the adapter",
    "knows about the affected set at the call site — so the case is the same case in",
    "every language. `bindings` then gives the concrete call for each adapter that can",
    "express that situation. A case with no binding for an adapter is NOT APPLICABLE to",
    "it and the runner MUST report it as such by name; it must never be silently",
    "skipped, or the count of cases passed stops meaning anything.",
    "",
    "target_shape is the one thing every adapter can answer without querying the",
    "resource:",
    "  container  — the target is the system's structure/control plane, not members of it",
    "  predicate  — the affected set is described by a filter, not enumerated",
    "  enumerated — the adapter holds the actual list of affected entities"
  ],
  "spec_section": "4.2",
  "ticket": "RFX-131",
  "broad_min": 20,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "container/schema",
      "given": {
        "target_shape": "container",
        "container": "schema",
        "note": "drops the container of tables, not rows in one"
      },
      "expect": {
        "blast_radius": "systemic"
      },
      "bindings": {
        "claude": {
          "tool": "Bash",
          "tool_input": {
            "command": "psql -c 'DROP SCHEMA public CASCADE'"
          }
        },
        "wordpress": {
          "ability": "db/drop-schema",
          "input": {
            "schema": "wp"
          },
          "trusted_scope": "container"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "container/filesystem-root",
      "given": {
        "target_shape": "container",
        "container": "runtime"
      },
      "expect": {
        "blast_radius": "systemic"
      },
      "bindings": {
        "claude": {
          "tool": "Bash",
          "tool_input": {
            "command": "rm -rf /"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "container/site-wide-config",
      "given": {
        "target_shape": "container",
        "container": "configuration",
        "note": "changes what the system is, for every entity in it. No name signal reaches this one, which is why the DECLARATION path exists."
      },
      "expect": {
        "blast_radius": "systemic"
      },
      "bindings": {
        "wordpress": {
          "ability": "core/flush-rewrites",
          "input": {},
          "trusted_scope": "container"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "container/access-control",
      "given": {
        "target_shape": "container",
        "container": "access_control",
        "note": "changes who may act. Reached by the NAME path (SYSTEMIC_SEGMENTS), no declaration."
      },
      "expect": {
        "blast_radius": "systemic"
      },
      "bindings": {
        "wordpress": {
          "ability": "core/reset-all-roles",
          "input": {}
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "predicate/whole-table",
      "given": {
        "target_shape": "predicate",
        "predicate": "every row in one table"
      },
      "expect": {
        "blast_radius": "broad"
      },
      "bindings": {
        "claude": {
          "tool": "Bash",
          "tool_input": {
            "command": "psql -c 'TRUNCATE TABLE wp_postmeta'"
          }
        },
        "wordpress": {
          "ability": "core/truncate-postmeta",
          "input": {}
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "predicate/no-where-clause",
      "given": {
        "target_shape": "predicate",
        "predicate": "statement with no filter"
      },
      "expect": {
        "blast_radius": "broad"
      },
      "bindings": {
